    `the spouse has a social security number valid for employment` IS FALSE
    `a spouse died in either of the two preceding years`      IS TRUE
    `the taxpayer remarried before the close of the year`     IS FALSE
    `a joint return could have been made for the year of that death` IS TRUE

`Elena` MEANS `2026 for a taxpayer aged` 45 `with marriage` `widowed in 2025` `income` (`income of wages` 50000 `and` 0 `interest` 0 `pensions` 0 `social security` 0 `business` 0 `less` 0 `FICA` 3825 `withheld` 2000) `people` (LIST (`a child at home aged` 12))
#ASSERT `the filing status` `Elena` EQUALS `surviving spouse`
-- Taxable income 50,000 - 32,200 = 17,800; Table 1: 1,780.
#ASSERT `the regular tax` `Elena` EQUALS 1780

-- Lena, 38, still married but living apart: she files separately, her son (8) lives with her all year, she pays over half
-- the cost of the home, and her husband has not lived there in the last 6 months. s 7703(b): not married; head of household.
`married but living apart` MEANS `Marriage` WITH
    `married at the close of the year or at the spouse's death` IS TRUE
    `the spouse died during the year`                         IS FALSE
    `legally separated under a decree of divorce or of separate maintenance` IS FALSE
    `the spouse was a nonresident alien at some time in the year` IS FALSE
    `the spouse was a member of the household in the last 6 months of the year` IS FALSE
    `the spouses lived apart at all times during the year`   IS FALSE
    `the spouses had the same household as their home at the close of the year` IS FALSE
    `the spouses make a joint return`                         IS FALSE
    `the spouse makes a separate return`                      IS TRUE
    `the spouse itemizes deductions on a separate return`     IS FALSE
    `the spouse's age at the close of the year`               IS 40
    `the spouse is blind`                                     IS FALSE
    `the spouse has gross income`                             IS TRUE
    `the spouse is the dependent of another taxpayer`         IS FALSE
    `the spouse has a social security number valid for employment` IS TRUE
    `a spouse died in either of the two preceding years`      IS FALSE
    `the taxpayer remarried before the close of the year`     IS FALSE
    `a joint return could have been made for the year of that death` IS FALSE

`Lena` MEANS `2026 for a taxpayer aged` 38 `with marriage` `married but living apart` `income` (`income of wages` 28000 `and` 0 `interest` 0 `pensions` 0 `social security` 0 `business` 0 `less` 0 `FICA` 2142 `withheld` 500) `people` (LIST (`a child at home aged` 8))
#ASSERT `treated as not married under s 7703(b)` `Lena`
#ASSERT `the filing status` `Lena` EQUALS `head of household`
-- s 32(d)(2)(B): married (s 7703(a)) and not filing jointly, but living with her son and not with her husband in the last 6
-- months: the credit is not barred. One child: 4,426.80 less 15.98% x (28,000 - 23,890) = 656.778: 3,770.022.
#ASSERT `the s 32(d) joint return condition is met` `Lena`
#ASSERT `the s 32 credit` `Lena` EQUALS 3770.022

§ `Dependents`

-- A 17-year-old is a qualifying child (s 152(c)) and counts for the EITC, but not for the s 24 child credit (s 24(c)(1)):
-- $500 under s 24(h)(4) instead.
`Hana, with a son of 17` MEANS `2026 for a taxpayer aged` 42 `with marriage` `no marriage` `income` (`income of wages` 45000 `and` 0 `interest` 0 `pensions` 0 `social security` 0 `business` 0 `less` 0 `FICA` 3442.5 `withheld` 2500) `people` (LIST (`a child at home aged` 17))
#ASSERT `the number of qualifying children for the s 24 credit` `Hana, with a son of 17` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the number of other dependents for the s 24 credit` `Hana, with a son of 17` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the s 24 credit before the tax limitation` `Hana, with a son of 17` EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `the number of qualifying children under s 32(b)` `Hana, with a son of 17` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the refundable portion of the s 24 credit under s 24(d)` `Hana, with a son of 17` EQUALS 0

-- A mother the taxpayer supports, with gross income $4,000 (below the $5,300 of s 152(d)(1)(B)), is a qualifying relative;
-- with $6,000 she is not.
#ASSERT `a dependent of the taxpayer` `Alex` (`a supported mother with gross income` 4000)
#ASSERT (NOT `a dependent of the taxpayer` `Alex` (`a supported mother with gross income` 6000))
-- She qualifies Alex as head of household under s 2(b)(1)(B) though she lives elsewhere.
#ASSERT `a parent who qualifies the taxpayer as head of household under s 2(b)(1)(B)` `Alex` (`a supported mother with gross income` 4000)

-- s 24(b): modified AGI of 410,500 on a joint return is 10,500 above 400,000: 11 x $50 = $550.
`a high-earning couple` MEANS `2026 for a taxpayer aged` 50 `with marriage` (`married to a spouse aged` 50 `making a joint return` TRUE) `income` (`income of wages` 300000 `and` 110500 `interest` 0 `pensions` 0 `social security` 0 `business` 0 `less` 0 `FICA` 0 `withheld` 0) `people` (LIST (`a child at home aged` 10))
#ASSERT `the s 24(b) reduction` `a high-earning couple` EQUALS 550
#ASSERT `the s 24 credit before the tax limitation` `a high-earning couple` EQUALS 1650

§ `A dependent's own return`

-- Mia, 20, a student whom her parents claim: wages $5,000. s 63(c)(5): basic standard deduction min(16,100, 450 + 5,000) =
-- 5,450. s 6012(a)(1)(C): unearned income 0, gross income 5,000 not above 5,450; exception (i): 5,000 < 0 + 5,450. None.
`a dependent student` MEANS `Taxable year` WITH
    `the calendar year`                                       IS 2026
    `the taxpayer's age at the close of the year`             IS 20
    `the taxpayer is blind`                                   IS FALSE
    `the taxpayer was a nonresident alien at some time in the year` IS FALSE
    `the taxpayer is a dependent of another taxpayer`         IS TRUE
    `the taxpayer is a qualifying child of another taxpayer`  IS TRUE
    `the taxpayer has a social security number valid for employment` IS TRUE
    `the taxpayer's principal place of abode was in the United States for more than half the year` IS TRUE
    `the taxpayer furnished over half the cost of maintaining the household` IS FALSE
    `marriage`                                                IS `no marriage`
    `people`                                                  IS `nobody`
    `income`                                                  IS (`income of wages` 5000 `and` 0 `interest` 0 `pensions` 0 `social security` 0 `business` 0 `less` 0 `FICA` 382.5 `withheld` 200)
#ASSERT `the standard deduction` `a dependent student` EQUALS 5450
#ASSERT `whether s 6012 requires a return` `a dependent student` EQUALS `answered` `no return is required`
#ASSERT `the s 32 credit` `a dependent student` EQUALS 0

-- The same student with $1,500 of interest and no wages: unearned income 1,500 exceeds 1,350, so s 6012(a)(1)(C)(i)(I) shuts
-- off the exceptions and a return is required on any gross income at or above the zero exemption amount ((D)(ii)).
`a dependent student with interest` MEANS `Taxable year` WITH
    `the calendar year`                                       IS 2026
    `the taxpayer's age at the close of the year`             IS 20
    `the taxpayer is blind`                                   IS FALSE
    `the taxpayer was a nonresident alien at some time in the year` IS FALSE
    `the taxpayer is a dependent of another taxpayer`         IS TRUE
    `the taxpayer is a qualifying child of another taxpayer`  IS TRUE
    `the taxpayer has a social security number valid for employment` IS TRUE
    `the taxpayer's principal place of abode was in the United States for more than half the year` IS TRUE
    `the taxpayer furnished over half the cost of maintaining the household` IS FALSE
    `marriage`                                                IS `no marriage`
    `people`                                                  IS `nobody`
    `income`                                                  IS (`income of wages` 0 `and` 0 `interest` 1500 `pensions` 0 `social security` 0 `business` 0 `less` 0 `FICA` 0 `withheld` 0)
#ASSERT `the exceptions are shut off by s 6012(a)(1)(C)` `a dependent student with interest`
#ASSERT `whether s 6012 requires a return` `a dependent student with interest` EQUALS `answered` `a return is required`
-- 1,500 of unearned income is under the 2,700 s 1(g) screen: covered. Standard deduction 1,350; taxable income 150; tax 15.
#ASSERT `the regular tax` `a dependent student with interest` EQUALS 15

