#ASSERT `the regular tax` `a high earner` EQUALS 394000.25

§ `s 6013 -- joint returns`

-- s 6013(a)(1): if the spouse was a nonresident alien at any time in the year, no joint return may be made, and the couple
-- files separately.
`married to a nonresident alien` MEANS `Marriage` WITH
    `married at the close of the year or at the spouse's death` IS TRUE
    `the spouse died during the year`                         IS FALSE
    `legally separated under a decree of divorce or of separate maintenance` IS FALSE
    `the spouse was a nonresident alien at some time in the year` IS TRUE
    `the spouse was a member of the household in the last 6 months of the year` IS TRUE
    `the spouses lived apart at all times during the year`   IS FALSE
    `the spouses had the same household as their home at the close of the year` IS TRUE
    `the spouses make a joint return`                         IS TRUE
    `the spouse makes a separate return`                      IS FALSE
    `the spouse itemizes deductions on a separate return`     IS FALSE
    `the spouse's age at the close of the year`               IS 33
    `the spouse is blind`                                     IS FALSE
    `the spouse has gross income`                             IS FALSE
    `the spouse is the dependent of another taxpayer`         IS FALSE
    `the spouse has a social security number valid for employment` IS FALSE
    `a spouse died in either of the two preceding years`      IS FALSE
    `the taxpayer remarried before the close of the year`     IS FALSE
    `a joint return could have been made for the year of that death` IS FALSE

`Omar` MEANS `2026 for a taxpayer aged` 34 `with marriage` `married to a nonresident alien` `income` (`income of wages` 52000 `and` 0 `interest` 0 `pensions` 0 `social security` 0 `business` 0 `less` 0 `FICA` 0 `withheld` 0) `people` `nobody`
#ASSERT (NOT `a joint return may be made under s 6013(a)` `Omar`)
-- s 2(b)(2)(B) makes him "not married" for head of household, but he has no qualifying person: married filing separately.
#ASSERT `the filing status` `Omar` EQUALS `married filing separately`
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`the permission to make a joint return` `Omar` 105) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 200)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH by the husband and wife, "a joint return was made although a spouse was a nonresident alien during the year"
#TRACE `the permission to make a joint return` `Omar` 105 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the husband and wife` DOES `make a single return jointly` AT 60

-- s 6013(b)(2)(A): from a due date of 15 April 2027, three years run to 15 April 2030, which is 1,096 days (2028 is a leap
-- year). A switch on day 1,000 is within the permission.
#ASSERT `days from the due date to the end of the s 6013(b)(2)(A) period` (`the calendar date` 15 4 2027) EQUALS 1096
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`the permission to switch to a joint return` `the Garcia family` FALSE (`days from the due date to the end of the s 6013(b)(2)(A) period` (`the calendar date` 15 4 2027))) 0 (LIST EVENT `the husband and wife` `make a joint return after filing a separate return` 1000) EQUALS FULFILLED
